From 75b2cd0e8463a51469309021c36bb13a6de0ab59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michele Dipace <kaffeine1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 03:20:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] m68kemu: an optional engine under the interpreter, selected
 by M68KEMU_CPU

m68kemu.library can run the 68k code between library calls on an engine
that implements the kaffeine-jit68 interface, version 1
(kaffeine-jit68-abi-v1.h). The interpreter stays the reference: every CPU
of a run is still a Moira CPU, which keeps the registers the thunks use,
takes every exception and interrupt and makes every library call. With
M68KEMU_CPU=jit or auto each of the three execution loops tries an engine
slice first; whatever instruction the engine stops at without executing
it (an A-line call, one it declines, one that raises an exception, one it
cannot fetch) is one step of the interpreter.

Without M68KEMU_CPU nothing of this runs.

- m68kemu_jit.c: the selection, the engine's map of the program's memory
  (first page, CIA and custom chip pages, the bitplane mirror), the
  invalidation, two message lines, the end.
- m68kemu_moira.cpp: an engine CPU per interpreter CPU, the slice, the
  two access callbacks; invalidation at CINV, CPUSH and the exec cache
  calls.
- m68kemu_run.c: the selection before the loader in RunHunk and RunFile;
  a refused run returns -1 with ERROR_INVALID_RESIDENT_LIBRARY.
- m68kemu_memory.c, m68kemu_m68klib.c, m68kemu_thunks.c: invalidation
  where the library writes 68k code; the engine's end in
  M68KEmu_DestroyContext.
- m68kemu.conf: 1.2.
---
